message: If you use this work, please cite it as below.
title: "Exactly when 6H misses a move in the 547/727 prime race"
abstract: "For starting heights from one million through one billion, the paper determines exactly which heights miss a gain or a loss for each deadline factor of at least six. At a factor of six there are 5,372,773 exceptional integer starts. These finite results follow from prime arithmetic. The earlier obstruction at arbitrarily large heights assumes Dirichlet GRH."
